##########Final Log:{"Question": {"task": "36 children were riding on the bus. At the bus stop 68 children got off the bus while some more got on the bus. Then there were 12 children altogether on the bus. How many more children got off the bus than those that got on?", "step": "", "answer": "24"}, "Answer": "24", "Step": "", "All_answers": [{"Math Solver8G9q": ["None."], "Mathematical Analyst5prY": ["## Problem solving process analysis\n\nThere were {initial_children} children initially on the bus.\nAt the bus stop, {got_off} children got off the bus.\nSome children got on the bus, let's call this number {got_on}.\nAfter all the activity, there were {final_children} children on the bus.\n\nWe can set up the equation:\n{initial_children} - {got_off} + {got_on} = {final_children}\nSo {got_on} = {final_children} - {initial_children} + {got_off}\n\nThe question asks for how many more children got off than got on:\n{difference} = {got_off} - {got_on}\n\n## Actual analysis and solution process\n\nIn this question:\n- {initial_children} = 36\n- {got_off} = 68\n- {final_children} = 12\n\nFirst, let's find how many children got on the bus:\n- 36 - 68 + got_on = 12\n- -32 + got_on = 12\n- got_on = 12 + 32 = 44\n\nNow, the difference between children who got off and those who got on:\n- Difference = 68 - 44 = 24\n\nThe answer is 24"], "Programming Expert3jZX": ["```python\ndef children_difference():\n    initial_children = 36\n    got_off = 68\n    final_children = 12\n    \n    # Calculate how many children got on the bus\n    # Equation: initial - got_off + got_on = final\n    # got_on = final - initial + got_off\n    got_on = final_children - initial_children + got_off\n    \n    # Calculate how many more children got off than got on\n    difference = got_off - got_on\n    \n    return difference\n\nanswer = children_difference()\n```\nthe answer is 24"], "Inspector46zf": ["Looking at this problem, I need to verify the logic and calculation.\n\n## My Solving Process\n\n**G