##########Final Log:{"Question": {"task": "Paul got a box of 440 crayons for his birthday. During the school year he gave 111 crayons to his friends while he lost 106 crayons. How many crayons did he have left?", "step": "", "answer": "223"}, "Answer": "223", "Step": "", "All_answers": [{"Math Solver8G9q": ["None."], "Mathematical Analyst5prY": ["## Problem solving process analysis\n\nPaul originally had {original_crayons} crayons.\nHe gave away {given_away} crayons to his friends.\nHe lost {lost} crayons.\nSo the number of crayons remaining {remaining} is the original number minus the crayons given away minus the crayons lost.\nThe answer is {remaining} = {original_crayons} - {given_away} - {lost}.\n\n## Actual analysis and solution process\n\nIn this question, {original_crayons} = 440, {given_away} = 111, and {lost} = 106.\nSo the number of crayons remaining is 440 - 111 - 106 = 440 - 217 = 223.\nThe answer is 223"], "Programming Expert3jZX": ["```python\ndef crayons_left():\n    original_crayons = 440\n    crayons_given_away = 111\n    crayons_lost = 106\n    remaining_crayons = original_crayons - crayons_given_away - crayons_lost\n    return remaining_crayons\n\nanswer = crayons_left()\n```\nthe answer is 223"], "Inspector46zf": ["Looking at this problem, I need to find how many crayons Paul has left after giving some away and losing some.\n\nStep-by-step solution:\n1. Paul started with 440 crayons\n2. He gave away 111 crayons\n3. He lost 106 crayons\n4. To find remaining crayons: 440 - 111 - 106\n\nCalculation:\n440 - 111 = 329\n329 - 106 = 223\n\nOr equivalently: 440 - (111 + 106) = 440 - 217 = 223\n\nVerification of the agents' responses:\n- Agent 5prY's mathematical analysis: Correctly calculated 440 - 111 - 106 = 223 \u2713\n- Agent 3jZX's code: Correctly implements the formula and returns 223 \u2713\n\nBoth agents provided the correct answer.\n\nThe answer is 223"], "Math Solver4Bp9": ["Looking at this problem, I need to find how many crayons Paul has left